[{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find the line passing through each of the following pairs of points giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,13)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4,-6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,-17)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2p,4q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,\\frac1p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac1p,p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\ne-1,0,1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{7-5}{1-2}=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-5=-2(x-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore2x+y=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{13-4}{4-1}=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-4=3(x-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore-3x+y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{1+3}{5+1}=\\frac23\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+3=\\frac23(x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore-2x+3y=-7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{-17+6}{-2+4}=-\\frac{11}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+6=-\\frac{11}2(x+4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore11x+2y=-56\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{4q-q}{2p-p}=\\frac{3q}p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-q=\\frac{3q}p(x-p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow py-pq=3qx-3pq\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore3qx-py=2pq\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{p-\\frac1p}{\\frac1p-p}=\\frac{p^2-1}{1-p^2}=-\\frac{p^2-1}{p^2-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-\\frac1p=-(x-p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y-\\frac1p=-x+p\\Rightarrow y+x=p+\\frac1p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore px+py=p^2+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>State both the gradient of the line and the gradient of a line which is perpendicular to each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x+6y=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3y-2x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x+8y=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7y-5x-2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20x+17y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6y=-3x+7\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac12x+\\frac72\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3y=2x+1\\Rightarrow y=\\frac23x+\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac23\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=-\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8y=-2x+11\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac14x+\\frac{11}8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=-\\frac14\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7y=5x+2\\Rightarrow y=\\frac57x+\\frac27\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac57\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=-\\frac75\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"17y=-20x+3\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac{20}{17}x+\\frac3{17}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=-\\frac{20}{17}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=\\frac{17}{20}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"by=-ax+c\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac abx+\\frac cb\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=-\\frac ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=\\frac ba\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>For each of the following pairs of lines, determine if they are perpendicular to each other:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x+3y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac32x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-5y+10=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24x+12y=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12y+24x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-4x+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4y-x=28\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"bx-ay=q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x+3y=1\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac23x+\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac23\\times-\\frac32\\ne-1\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> not perpendicular.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-5y-10=0\\Rightarrow y=\\frac15x+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac15\\times5\\ne-1\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> not perpendicular.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24x+12y=16\\Rightarrow y=-2x+\\frac43\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12y+24x=1\\Rightarrow y=-2x+\\frac1{12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\\times-2\\ne-1\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> not perpendicular (they are parallel).</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac x2+\\frac y8=1\\Rightarrow y=-4x+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4y-x=28\\Rightarrow y=\\frac14x+7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\\times\\frac14=-1\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> perpendicular.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=p\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac abx+\\frac pb\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"bx-ay=q\\Rightarrow y=\\frac bax-\\frac qa\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac ab\\times\\frac ba=-1\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> perpendicular.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>For the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"px+qy=r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers find a relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that the two lines are</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Parallel.</p></li><li><p>Perpendicular.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac abx+\\frac cb\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"px+qy=r\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac pqx+\\frac rq\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac ab=\\frac pq\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"aq=bp\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac abx+\\frac cb\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"px+qy=r\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac pqx+\\frac rq\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac ab\\times-\\frac pq=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{ap}{bq}=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ap=-bq\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Find the midpoint between each of these pairs of points:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-8,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-7,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac72,12)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2p,3q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,\\frac1p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac1p,p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\ne-1,0,1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-4+4}2,\\frac{3+9}2)=(0,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{1+6}2,\\frac{7-5}2)=(\\frac72,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-8-2}2,\\frac{10-1}2)=(-5,\\frac92)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-7+\\frac72}2,\\frac{-2+12}2)=(-\\frac74,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{p+2p}2,\\frac{q+3q}2)=(\\frac32p,2q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{p+\\frac1p}2,\\frac{p+\\frac1p}2)=(\\frac12p+\\frac1{2p},\\frac12p+\\frac1{2p})\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>For each of the following, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given the point which lies on the line:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2y-5x=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x-3y+20=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times4-5k=16\\Rightarrow k=-\\frac85\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4(2k)-3(k)+20=0\\Rightarrow5k=-20\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow k=-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Find the perpendicular bisector of the each of the following points giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-6,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-9,11)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2p,3q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{1-5}{6+2}=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-2+6}2,\\frac{5+1}2)=(2,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-3=2(x-2)\\Rightarrow y-3=2x-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow2x-y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{8-5}{6-3}=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{3+6}2,\\frac{5+8}2)=(\\frac92,\\frac{13}2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-\\frac{13}2=-1(x-\\frac92)\\Rightarrow y-\\frac{13}2=-x+\\frac92\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x+y=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{10-2}{4-1}=\\frac83\" data-display=\"false\"></span> midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{1+4}2,\\frac{2+10}2)=(\\frac52,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-6=-\\frac38(x-\\frac52)\\Rightarrow-8y+48=3x-\\frac{15}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow8y+3x=\\frac{111}2\\Rightarrow6x+16y=111\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{-5-2}{-1+6}=-\\frac75\" data-display=\"false\"></span> midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-6-1}2,\\frac{2-5}2)=(-\\frac72,-\\frac32)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+\\frac32=\\frac57(x+\\frac72)\\Rightarrow7y+\\frac{21}2=5x+\\frac{35}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow5x-7y=-7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{-2-11}{-1+9}=-\\frac{13}8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-9-1}2,\\frac{11-2}2)=(-5,\\frac92)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-\\frac92=\\frac8{13}(x+5)\\Rightarrow13y-\\frac{117}2=8x+40\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow13y-8x=\\frac{197}2\\Rightarrow16x-26y=-197\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{3q-q}{2p-p}=\\frac{2q}p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{p+2p}2,\\frac{q+3q}2)=(\\frac32p,2q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-2q=-\\frac p{2q}(x-\\frac32p)\\Rightarrow2qy-4q^2=-px+\\frac32p^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow4qy-8q^2=-2px+3p^2\\Rightarrow2px+4qy=8q^2+3p^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the straight line which is parallel to the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2y-x=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Give your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac12x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-4=\\frac12(x+1)\\Rightarrow2y-8=x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x-2y=-9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the straight line which is perpendicular to the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6y+2x-11=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Give your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac13x-\\frac{11}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-3=3(x-2)\\Rightarrow y-3=3x-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow3x-y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Find the angle (in degrees to 1 decimal place) between each of the following pairs of lines:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2x-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-5x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan^{-1}(\\frac21)=63.4^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between lines: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"63.4^\\circ-0^\\circ=63.4^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan^{-1}(\\frac31)=71.6^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan^{-1}(\\frac41)=76.0^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between lines: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"76.0^\\circ-71.6^\\circ=4.4^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan^{-1}(\\frac51)=78.7^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ+\\tan^{-1}(\\frac11)=135^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between lines: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"135^\\circ-78.7^\\circ=56.3^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2x-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ+\\tan^{-1}(\\frac21)=153.4^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-3x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ+\\tan^{-1}(\\frac51)=168.7^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Angle between lines: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"168.7^\\circ-153.4^\\circ=15.3^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Find the area of the triangle bounded by the coordinate axes and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2y+x-11=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Meets the axes at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,\\frac{11}2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(11,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=\\frac12\\times\\frac{11}2\\times11=\\frac{121}4\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Find the area in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the triangle bounded by the coordinate axes and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ky+3x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant.</p>","steps":["<p>Meets the axes at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,\\frac2k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac23,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=\\frac12\\times\\frac2k\\times\\frac23=\\frac2{3k}\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The three points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,11)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are all corners of a triangle. By considering the gradients of the lines passing through each of the pairs of points, show that it is a right-angled triangle.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{-2-11}{4-3}=-13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=\\frac{1+2}{-2-4}=-\\frac36=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_3=\\frac{1-11}{-2-3}=\\frac{10}5=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So the line passing through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is perpendicular to the line passing through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,11)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so it must be a right-angled triangle.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The three points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,-7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are all corners of a triangle. By considering the distances between each of the pairs of points, show that it is a right-angled triangle and hence find the area of the triangle.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(-1-5)^2+(8-10)^2}=\\sqrt{36+4}=\\sqrt{40}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(4+1)^2+(-7-8)^2}=\\sqrt{25+225}=\\sqrt{250}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(4-5)^2+(-7-10)^2}=\\sqrt{1+289}=\\sqrt{290}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\sqrt{40})^2+(\\sqrt{250})^2=(\\sqrt{290})^2\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> a right-angled triangle.  Area: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times\\sqrt{40}\\times\\sqrt{250}=50\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2y-7x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ky+6x=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are perpendicular to each other.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac72x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac6kx+\\frac{10}k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac72=\\frac k6\\Rightarrow k=21\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A line perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+2x=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2x+9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so gradient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{7-6}{1-p}=\\frac12\\Rightarrow1-p=2\\Rightarrow p=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Two points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(p,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(5,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have a perpendicular bisector with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3y+x=15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Midpoint: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{p+5}2,\\frac{q-2}2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Midpoint in perpendicular bisector:  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(\\frac{q-2}2)+(\\frac{p+5}2)=15\\Rightarrow3(q-2)+p+5=30\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow p+3q=31\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Gradients:  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-\\frac13x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3=\\frac{q+2}{5-p}\\Rightarrow3(5-p)=q+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow15-3p=q+2\\Rightarrow3p+q=13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Solving: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=1,q=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-5,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(10,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-15,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are collinear.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{13-10}{10+5}=\\frac3{15}=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=\\frac{5-10}{-15-10}=\\frac5{25}=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Since both gradients are the same and they have a common point, then they are collinear.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>Find the value(s) of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-15,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are collinear.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3k,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(7,\\frac32)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are collinear.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{3-9}{3+15}=\\frac6{-18}=-\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=\\frac{-5-3}{k-3}=-\\frac8{k-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Since both gradients are the same  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac13=-\\frac8{k-3}\\Rightarrow k-3=24\\Rightarrow k=27\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{3-k}{-3k-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=\\frac{\\frac32-3}{7+3k}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Since both gradients are the same  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{3-k}{-3k-1}=\\frac{\\frac32-3}{7+3k}\\Rightarrow(3-k)(7+3k)=-\\frac32(-3k-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow-3k^2+2k+21=\\frac92k+\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow-3k^2-\\frac52k+\\frac{39}2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow k=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{13}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>Three points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.03/questions/assets/diagrams/q20.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of the perpendicular bisector of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the equation of the perpendicular bisector of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where the two perpendicular bisectors intersect.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance between the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and each of the three points.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{2-10}{5+3}=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{5-3}2,\\frac{2+10}2)=(1,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-6=1(x-1)\\Rightarrow y=x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_1=\\frac{2-6}{5-9}=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_2=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{5+9}2,\\frac{2+6}2)=(7,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-4=-1(x-7)\\Rightarrow y=-x+11\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+5=-x+11\\Rightarrow x=3,y=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>AP: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(3+3)^2+(8-10)^2}=\\sqrt{36+4}=2\\sqrt{10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  BP: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(3-5)^2+(8-2)^2}=\\sqrt{4+36}=2\\sqrt{10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  CP: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(3-9)^2+(8-6)^2}=\\sqrt{36+4}=2\\sqrt{10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>By considering the line that is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3y-4x=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(11,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the shortest distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(11,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3y-4x=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac43x+\\frac53\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=-\\frac34\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-8=-\\frac34(x-11)\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac34x+\\frac{65}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Point of intersection: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac43x+\\frac53=-\\frac34x+\\frac{65}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac{175}{12}=\\frac{25}{12}x\\Rightarrow x=7,y=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Distance between points: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(11-7)^2+(8-11)^2}=\\sqrt{16+9}=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>Three points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(10,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(5,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(20,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(15,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> form the vertices of a trapezium.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.03/questions/assets/diagrams/q22.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>the equation of the line passing through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the equation of the line passing through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given that it is parallel to the line passing through points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the distances between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> &amp; <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> &amp; <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the equation of the line which is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the shortest distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the area of the trapezium <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_{AB}=\\frac{4-10}{5-10}=\\frac65\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_{BC}=\\frac{1-4}{20-5}=-\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_{AB}m_{BC}\\ne-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so not perpendicular</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-4=-\\frac15(x-5)\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac15x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Gradient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-10=-\\frac15(x-10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=-\\frac15x+12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=-\\frac15\\times15+12=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>AD: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(15-10)^2+(9-10)^2}=\\sqrt{25+1}=\\sqrt{26}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  BC: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(1-4)^2+(20-5)^2}=\\sqrt{9+225}=3\\sqrt{26}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-10=5(x-10)\\Rightarrow y=5x-40\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p>Intersection:  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac15x+5=5x-40\\Rightarrow\\frac{26}5x=45\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{225}{26},y=\\frac{85}{26}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(10-\\frac{225}{26})^2+(10-\\frac{85}{26})^2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1225}{676}+\\frac{30625}{676}}=\\frac{35}{26}\\sqrt{26}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">h)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(\\frac{35}{26}\\sqrt{26})(3\\sqrt{26}+\\sqrt{26})=70\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-6,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-4,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> form a quadrilateral.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.03/questions/assets/diagrams/q23.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the distances between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are the same.</p></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is perpendicular to the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Show that the possible coordinates of the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> satisfy the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+3y=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Distance AB: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(3-2)^2+(1-(-6))^2}=5\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Distance BC: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(3-8)^2+(1-(-4))^2}=5\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> distances are the same</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Line going through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-2=\\frac{8-2}{-4-(-6)}(x-6)\\Rightarrow y-2=3(x+6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Line going through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-3=-\\frac13(x-1)\\Rightarrow3y-9=-x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow3y+x=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.03-q24","number":24,"question":"<p>Four points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(-3,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(2,-\\frac35)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(4,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(-1,\\frac{18}5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> form a quadrilateral. By considering the diagonals only, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, determine its type.</p>","steps":["<p>Midpoint of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{-3+4}2,\\frac{-1+4}2)=(\\frac12,\\frac32)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Midpoint of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{2-1}2,\\frac{-\\frac35+\\frac{18}5}2)=(\\frac12,\\frac32)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Gradient of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{4-(-1)}{4-(-3)}=\\frac57\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Gradient of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=\\frac{\\frac{18}5-(-\\frac35)}{-1-2}=-\\frac75\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are perpendicular bisectors of each other  Distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(-1-4)^2+(-3-4)^2}=\\sqrt{74}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(\\frac{18}5+\\frac35)^2+(-1-2)^2}=\\frac35\\sqrt{74}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  As the distances are different, it is not a square.  So it must be a rhombus.</p>"]}]